# Security, privacy and tenant safety

Read `docs/security/SECURITY_PRIVACY_SAFETY_RULES.md`.

- Deny by default on missing identity, tenant, role, assignment, consent or entitlement.
- Require positive and cross-tenant negative tests for tenant-sensitive behavior.
- Clients see only their own approved runtime data; coaches see only assigned-client permitted projections.
- Never expose service-role credentials or store secrets/personal data in prompts, logs, screenshots or evidence.
- Use synthetic data for development and demos.
- Raw staging/candidates are not client runtime truth; canonical promotion is never autonomous.
- Security claims require executed evidence, not file presence or agent self-assessment.